      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Melanoma in lighter skin tones is often recognized by the ABCDE rule, which covers asymmetry, border irregularity, color variation, diameter, and evolution. In darker skin tones, however, the presentation can be much trickier and often presents as a change in an existing mole or as a dark, non-blanching lesion. Dermatologists often look for signs like hyperpigmentation, scaling, or a change in the texture of the skin, which can be easily missed if one is not aware of the differences.",
